{"index": 93, "infinity-chat-info": {"form_id": 14, "question_id": "Q2"}, "annotations": [{"annotator_id": 1, "overall": 3, "meaning": 4, "form": 4}, {"annotator_id": 2, "overall": 2, "meaning": 2, "form": 2}, {"annotator_id": 3, "overall": 2, "meaning": 3, "form": 5}, {"annotator_id": 4, "overall": 3, "meaning": 2, "form": 3}, {"annotator_id": 5, "overall": 4, "meaning": 3, "form": 4}, {"annotator_id": 6, "overall": 4, "meaning": 1, "form": 5}, {"annotator_id": 7, "overall": 2, "meaning": 3, "form": 4}, {"annotator_id": 8, "overall": 1, "meaning": 2, "form": 2}], "edited": true, "similarity_calculation_results": {"pairwise": {"semantic_cosine_similarity": {"model": "qwen3-8b-embedding", "value": 0.5161556601524353}, "infomatch_sentence": {"precision": 0.5660196542739868, "recall": 0.5749527215957642, "f1": 0.5704512178981493}, "style_cosine_similarity": {"model": "styledistance", "value": 0.9899325370788574}, "bleu": 0.0233690629551113, "rouge_l": 0.15935334872979215}, "scalar": {"mtld": -62.585500626792054, "punctuation_density": -5.490678840312091, "function_word_density": -7.316725654133968, "paragraph_density": -0.4268754880001824, "total_length_chars": -313.0, "readability_flesch_kincaid_grade": -3.471710489276738, "emotion_intensity_diff": -0.028647684143348173, "emphasis_density": -0.6081123440536647, "list_density": -0.03419563321763819, "avg_concreteness": -0.0371957464828494, "word_freq_avg_zipf_frequency": -0.16288195097486025}, "distribution": {"punctuation": -0.09889405851392183, "pos_dist": -0.023572149133707563, "dep_dist": -0.05310414734626363, "function_words_js": -0.011050793507332802, "emotion_profile_js": -0.059421333944641344}, "binary": {"header_use": 1.0, "list_use": 1.0, "markdown_emphasis_use": 1.0, "form_opening_template": 1.0, "form_closing_template": 1.0}, "response_1": {"raw_text": "Sure — here's a pitch built around procedure rather than spectacle.\n\n## Premise and Cast\n\n**Title: The Extraction**\n\nProtagonist Jack \"The Ghost\" Griffin is a former Army Ranger turned **private security consultant**. He's hired by a wealthy tech mogul to extract his kidnapped daughter, a brilliant engineer named Emma, from a heavily fortified compound in a fictional Eastern European country.\n\n## The Setup\n\nJack agrees to take the job, but only after negotiating a hefty fee and insisting on bringing his own team. He assembles a group of skilled operatives:\n\n- a **former Navy SEAL**\n- a cybersecurity expert\n- a *local guide who knows the terrain*\n\nAs they plan, Jack and his team spend hours pouring over satellite imagery, blueprints of the compound, and intelligence reports on the kidnappers.\n\n## Going In\n\nThey arrive at the compound just after midnight, when the guards are least expecting it. They move stealthily through the compound, using **cover and concealment** to avoid detection. The cybersecurity expert hacks into the compound's security cameras, disabling them to create a blind spot for the team.\n\n## Where It Goes Wrong\n\nThe team reaches Emma's cell and finds her bound and gagged. Jack quickly frees her, and they make their way back to the extraction point. However, things start to go wrong when they're ambushed by a group of heavily armed reinforcements — the team fights bravely, but they're *outnumbered and outgunned*. They retreat to a nearby safe house, where they treat their wounded and reassess their situation.\n\n## The Turn\n\nThe team comes up with a new plan, using the local guide's knowledge of the terrain to outmaneuver the kidnappers. As they make their way back to the extraction point, they're met with a surprise: the tech mogul's security team, who have been tracking them from the beginning. Jack's old Army buddy vouches for them, and they're able to extract Emma safely. Emma is reunited with her father, who's overjoyed to have her back.\n\n## Where the Realism Lives\n\nThe team spends hours planning and preparing for the extraction, rather than rushing in without a plan. They're a group of **skilled operatives with diverse skill sets**, rather than a lone hero who can do everything, and the movie acknowledges the *physical and emotional toll of combat*. The final confrontation is a tense and realistic firefight, rather than a cartoonish showdown between the hero and the villain.\n\nThat's the shape of it — tell me if you'd rather see the beats expanded or the cast trimmed down.", "features": {"mtld": 93.9444069120581, "punctuation_density": 12.224938875305623, "function_word_density": 46.9437652811736, "paragraph_density": 4.156479217603912, "response_length_chars": 2536, "readability_flesch_kincaid_grade": 7.818075558009308, "emotion_intensity": 0.0993044376373291, "emphasis_density": 1.9559902200488997, "list_density": 0.7334963325183375, "avg_concreteness": 2.9184259351620945, "word_freq": {"avg_zipf_frequency": 5.600317848410757}, "punctuation": {"comma": 22, "period": 20, "dash": 3, "hyphen": 0, "semicolon": 0, "colon": 3, "exclamation": 0, "question": 0, "ellipsis": 0, "paren": 0, "quote": 2}, "pos_dist": {"ADJ": 0.08254716981132075, "ADP": 0.09433962264150944, "ADV": 0.04716981132075472, "AUX": 0.04009433962264151, "CCONJ": 0.04481132075471698, "DET": 0.12971698113207547, "NOUN": 0.22877358490566038, "PART": 0.030660377358490566, "PRON": 0.09433962264150944, "PROPN": 0.04481132075471698, "SCONJ": 0.018867924528301886, "VERB": 0.14150943396226415, "INTJ": 0.0023584905660377358}, "dep_dist": {"ROOT": 0.07311320754716981, "acl": 0.007075471698113208, "acomp": 0.007075471698113208, "advcl": 0.01179245283018868, "advmod": 0.05660377358490566, "agent": 0.0047169811320754715, "amod": 0.0660377358490566, "appos": 0.007075471698113208, "attr": 0.007075471698113208, "aux": 0.030660377358490566, "auxpass": 0.014150943396226415, "case": 0.01179245283018868, "cc": 0.054245283018867926, "ccomp": 0.014150943396226415, "compound": 0.04481132075471698, "conj": 0.049528301886792456, "det": 0.12971698113207547, "dobj": 0.06839622641509434, "mark": 0.007075471698113208, "nmod": 0.007075471698113208, "nsubj": 0.08018867924528301, "nsubjpass": 0.014150943396226415, "oprd": 0.0023584905660377358, "pcomp": 0.007075471698113208, "pobj": 0.07311320754716981, "poss": 0.030660377358490566, "prep": 0.07311320754716981, "prt": 0.009433962264150943, "relcl": 0.014150943396226415, "xcomp": 0.02122641509433962, "intj": 0.0023584905660377358}, "function_words": {"profile": {"article": 0.2916666666666667, "preposition": 0.20833333333333334, "cconj": 0.09895833333333333, "sconj": 0.041666666666666664, "pronoun": 0.203125, "auxiliary": 0.08854166666666667, "particle": 0.06770833333333333}}, "emotion_profile": {"neutral": 0.6758748618560992, "approval": 0.10273661968682739, "realization": 0.02696180154224828, "admiration": 0.00243098512711268, "annoyance": 0.010840027505967109, "disappointment": 0.020206046745540267, "optimism": 0.007949298455772035, "fear": 0.0024762183625546548, "pride": 0.0003270059296002886, "sadness": 0.008281737745200034, "relief": 0.001776144166565396, "excitement": 0.0025575338862679547, "disapproval": 0.006429190034776667, "disgust": 0.0010143123984302862, "joy": 0.001971963355639067, "surprise": 0.004159614945582611, "caring": 0.0038162393228184195, "embarrassment": 0.001193426833336781, "nervousness": 0.0027427626425091745, "desire": 0.0024263877336486357, "anger": 0.000998913141655269, "gratitude": 0.0002093045814929105, "confusion": 0.0258199290592693, "amusement": 0.0004331415307111205, "grief": 0.0007515764565253791, "love": 0.0006132345617415732, "remorse": 0.000767538403813443, "curiosity": 0.08423418398829405}, "header_use": true, "list_use": true, "markdown_emphasis_use": true, "form_label": {"opening_template": true, "closing_template": true}}}, "response_2": {"raw_text": "Certainly — taking this one in a grounded, city-scale direction instead.\n\n## The World\n\n**Title: \"Urban Reckoning\"** — **Genre: Action/Thriller**\n\n**Setting:** A sprawling metropolitan city, teeming with life, crime, and corporate greed. The city is a character in itself, a blend of towering skyscrapers, crowded streets, and *underprivileged neighborhoods*.\n\n## Act 1: The Catalyst\n\nWe meet our protagonist, Alex Torres, a mid-level data analyst working for a powerful tech company, **Apex Dynamics**. One evening, while working late, Alex accidentally uncovers a trove of incriminating data on Apex's involvement in illegal surveillance and unethical practices, including corrupt dealings with law enforcement. As he gathers evidence, he is noticed by a shadowy figure — a corporate enforcer named Marcus Reed, who works for Apex's security division.\n\n## Act 2: The Response\n\nAfter Alex's attempts to report his findings to a journalist are thwarted when he learns the journalist has been bought off, he decides to leak the information himself through social media. The release of the data sends shockwaves through the city, igniting *protests and stirring public outrage* against Apex Dynamics. He teams up with Mia, a former investigative journalist who lost her job due to corporate censorship, and they enlist a group of allies:\n\n- a **tech-savvy hacker**\n- a streetwise activist\n- a disillusioned ex-cop who knows the corrupt system\n\n## Act 3: The Confrontation\n\nApex retaliates by framing Alex for crimes he didn't commit and sending a squad of mercenaries after him and his team. There are no over-the-top explosions; instead, the tension builds through **realistic action sequences** — parkour through city streets, close calls in crowded areas, and technology-driven confrontations.\n\n## Act 4: The Climax\n\nApex's CEO, a charismatic yet ruthless character, orders Marcus to eliminate Alex and Mia. In a thrilling sequence that culminates in the corporate headquarters during a high-stakes shareholder meeting, Alex and his allies infiltrate the building to live-stream evidence of the company's misdeeds to the public. They face Marcus in a well-choreographed but realistic fight — one based more on *wits and resourcefulness* than sheer physical prowess.\n\n## Act 5: The Resolution\n\nWith the truth finally out in the open, public backlash forces government investigations into Apex Dynamics. The film ends with Alex and Mia standing together, hopeful yet aware of the ongoing fight against systemic corruption, and closes with a reminder that while the battle against corruption is far from over, **every small victory counts**. The story runs on *corporate accountability*, grassroots power, and the consequences of ethical choices.\n\nIf the corporate angle isn't what you're after, I can swap the antagonist or dial the scale up or down.", "features": {"mtld": 156.52990753885015, "punctuation_density": 17.715617715617714, "function_word_density": 39.62703962703963, "paragraph_density": 3.7296037296037294, "response_length_chars": 2849, "readability_flesch_kincaid_grade": 11.289786047286047, "emotion_intensity": 0.12795212178067727, "emphasis_density": 2.5641025641025643, "list_density": 0.6993006993006993, "avg_concreteness": 2.881230188679245, "word_freq": {"avg_zipf_frequency": 5.437435897435897}, "punctuation": {"comma": 32, "period": 17, "dash": 5, "hyphen": 10, "semicolon": 1, "colon": 9, "exclamation": 0, "question": 0, "ellipsis": 0, "paren": 0, "quote": 2}, "pos_dist": {"ADJ": 0.09728506787330317, "ADP": 0.11312217194570136, "ADV": 0.03619909502262444, "AUX": 0.02262443438914027, "CCONJ": 0.04072398190045249, "DET": 0.11990950226244344, "NOUN": 0.26244343891402716, "NUM": 0.01583710407239819, "PART": 0.02262443438914027, "PRON": 0.05656108597285068, "PROPN": 0.08597285067873303, "SCONJ": 0.01583710407239819, "VERB": 0.11085972850678733}, "dep_dist": {"ROOT": 0.06334841628959276, "acl": 0.00904977375565611, "advcl": 0.01809954751131222, "advmod": 0.024886877828054297, "agent": 0.0022624434389140274, "amod": 0.09728506787330317, "appos": 0.03619909502262444, "attr": 0.006787330316742082, "aux": 0.013574660633484163, "auxpass": 0.006787330